+# ee81661 milestone capture attribution correction
+
+This is a documentation-only correction to the report published in evidence commit
+`3c823a0182c4a7f69cf235fe020e435b712e6a5b`, `START-HERE.md`, step 6.
+The reviewed original report, screenshots, DOM, database checkpoints and checksum
+manifests remain unchanged. This erratum does not substitute a new capture.
+
+The original wording says: “Compared both notes, expanded authored narrative/provenance”.
+
+Correct attribution: Compared both notes and expanded their authored narratives.
+Captures 12/13 show expanded narratives; the inner uncertainty/provenance disclosures
+remain collapsed. Those captures do not independently demonstrate expanded provenance
+contents. Retained record/API/database evidence and code review have their separately
+stated scope; they must not be attributed to those collapsed browser disclosures.
+
+This correction adds no browser, API, database or runtime observation. It accompanies
+the repository-identity continuation fix and does not change the earlier evidence.
+Production execution remains disabled. No merge, deployment or external hosting is authorized.
